<title>POLAND: Polish Celuloza to start bourse trade April 25.</title>
<headline>Polish Celuloza to start bourse trade April 25.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish largest paper firm Celuloza Swiecie SA will start regular trade on the Warsaw Stock Exchange main market on April 25, the head of the bourse sessions department said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The first listing of the company (Celuloza Swiecie) will take place on April 25,&quot; Adam Maciejewski told Reuters.</p>
<p>On April 22 Celuloza Swiecie's shares offered in the undergoing public offer will be allotted at a special bourse session. The state treasury wants to sell 7.5 million shares at a minimum price of 15 zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
